# The tool image's build context (Dockerfile). It leaves out what belongs to one machine, and
# every paper's data, so the image is the same whether it is built from a clone or from an
# artifact archive, and knows no paper.

# Local state, which no archive carries:
.git
.venv
.gpap
.experiments
build
cpp/build
cpp/src/generated
gpap/lib
**/__pycache__
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
*.egg-info
.vscode
.claude
.superpowers

# The paper's files, which an artifact archive adds. The artifact layer (eval/artifact/Dockerfile)
# copies back exactly these, so inside it /opt/gpap is the archive:
artifact-data
MANIFEST.*
README-ARTIFACT.md
